    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0364" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg294"/>

                <head>No. 150.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Morton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 13,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 400.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The action of yourself and Mr. Vignaud, as
                    delegates to the international conference for the protection of submarine
                    cables, as reported in your dispatch No. 441 of the 10th ultimo, is approved by
                    the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
